================================================================================
LICENSING OF THIS FORK
================================================================================

This repository is licensed in its entirety under the Apache License 2.0.

Upstream Flowise was open core. 127 files were NOT Apache 2.0 — they were
governed by a separate FlowiseAI Inc Commercial License that forbids copying,
publishing, distributing, sublicensing and selling:

    packages/server/src/enterprise/      (126 files)
    packages/server/src/IdentityManager.ts

Those files have been DELETED from this fork. They are not present in this
repository, in any branch published from it, or in any artifact built from it.
Nothing has been relicensed: no fork can relicense code it does not own, and no
attempt to do so was made.

The functionality they provided — authentication, RBAC, SSO and multi-tenancy —
was reimplemented from scratch under Apache 2.0 in packages/server/src/identity/.
That reimplementation was derived exclusively from Apache-2.0 licensed sources
in this repository (principally packages/ui/, which contains no commercially
licensed files, and the permission call sites in packages/server/src/routes/).
The commercially licensed files were never read, decompiled, or otherwise
examined during its development.

The process, the prohibitions it operated under, and verifiable evidence for
both are documented in:

    docs/CLEANROOM-PROTOCOL.md      the binding process
    docs/CLEANROOM-ATTESTATION.md   the evidence, with re-runnable commands
    docs/SPEC-AUTH-RBAC.md          the interface specification and its citations

The attestation records a disclosed incident in which a malformed command
briefly exposed approximately twelve lines of one protected file, together with
the remediation applied. It is published rather than omitted.

Because upstream's Apache-2.0 authentication was deleted in Flowise 3.0 and
replaced by the commercial stack, simply removing those 127 files would have
produced an unauthenticated server. That is why they were replaced rather than
dropped.

See FORK.md for full details.

